# What must never reach the image.
#
# Two kinds of thing. The first is obvious: secrets and live data. `.env` holds
# the production secret key, and neural_log.db is everybody's logged days - both
# would be baked into a layer, and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull
# the image. The registry is public.
#
# The second is size. node_modules and .venv are hundreds of megabytes that the
# build regenerates anyway, and every one of them is a megabyte uploaded on
# every build.

# Secrets and live data
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.bak
*.db.*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.pem
*.key
backups/
deploy/known_hosts
artifacts/checklists/
artifacts/paths/
artifacts/checklist_items/
exports/

# Regenerated by the build
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Not needed at runtime
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.pytest_cache/
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Local run state
app_run.log
app_run.pid
frontend/vite.log
frontend/vite.pid

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
